    "body": "## Summary\n\nFix an existing `main` bug in the HF3FS L3 backend. MLA KV is replicated across TP ranks, but Mamba state is TP-sharded and `should_backup` makes every TP rank back up its own shard. On MLA models every rank collapses to rank 0's file and metadata, and the Mamba component key is `<key>_mamba` with no rank, so every rank writes the same entry and restores another rank's state.\n\nFollowing #43594 (the same fix for NIXL): on MLA models, Mamba component keys carry the TP rank (`<key>_mamba_{rank}_{size}`); KV and other pools keep their keys. Ranks still share one file and one metadata namespace, so each rank's shard gets its own pages in the shared file. `HiCacheHF3FS` now records the original TP rank before the MLA collapse and takes `tp_size` from the storage config. Existing rank-ambiguous Mamba entries read as misses.\n\nSplit out of #41907 so each storage backend is reviewed on its own.\n\n## Tests\n\n```bash\npython -m pytest -q test/registered/unit/mem_cache/test_hicache_hf3fs_mamba_keys.py\n```\n\n- New `test_mla_mamba_state_stays_per_rank`: two MLA TP ranks share one HF3FS file and metadata client, write the same page keys with different Mamba payloads, and must each read back their own.\n- This PR: 1 passed.\n- Negative control (same tree, rank tag disabled): the test fails, reading the other rank's payload.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38231178376](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38231178376)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38231178144](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38231178144)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38231178350](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38231178350)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
